From 1646ba22f9ad8ba709d3fdadfdcc3a3462435e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 04:57:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] p1-recommend-and-capture

P1 (days 8-21): recommendability assets and intent surfaces, on top of P0.

P1.1 First-party proof. content/job-cards.ts publishes five finished jobs -
neighbourhood, size, substrate, species, year and ONE measured result each -
and scripts/verify-job-cards.mjs fails the build the moment any figure stops
matching its case-study .mdx. Deliberately carries no photograph (none of the
five studies sets an image) and no customer name: the testimonial attributions
in the studies have no consent record in this repo, and the guard structurally
bans a name/quote field so nobody adds one quietly. JobCard/JobCardRail render
on the homepage, /case-studies, service pages, area pages and both new pages.

P1.2 The quote scorer becomes a weapon, without becoming a lead form. Answers
still never leave the browser; they now mirror into the URL (one char per
criterion) so a score can be reloaded, sent to a spouse, or sent back to the
contractor who wrote the quote. A separate, optional upload under the result
sends us the actual document (/api/quote-review to the estimating desk, never
stored, never filed as a lead). The page privacy copy was rewritten to match
rather than left contradicting itself.

P1.3 Papers become sales assets. content/quote-impact.ts adds one <=120-word
box per paper - what the reader should now require of their quote - signed by
the Ecowoods estimating desk, never an invented person. verify-quote-impact.mjs
enforces the word limit, that every paper has one, and that each box anchors to
a section that really exists. The papers themselves are untouched.

P1.4 32 area pages de-duplicated. The first paragraph was one shared 48-word
template with the city name substituted, sitting ABOVE the only unique block on
the page. CITY_CONTENT is now the lede; H1 leads with refinishing; each page
gains an area-scoped Service node with its own @id, a NAP block derived from
BUSINESS_NAP, and a local JobCard where a published job exists (4 of 32).

P1.5 Most-searched rail on the homepage, reaching the 8 commercial canonicals.

P1.6 Two new demand surfaces. /commercial (condo boards, property managers:
after-hours protocol, COI on request - not a fake PDF, bands itemised by area)
and /realtors (three-day pre-list screen and recoat on the published band, with
an explicit section on when we will say not to do it; prints as the seller
one-pager rather than advertising a download that does not exist). Both wired
into topic map, sitemap, llms.txt, chrome, and both guard allowlists.

P1.7 After-hours capture. lib/business-hours.ts derives opening hours from
BUSINESS_HOURS and knows the office clock; the chat widget now hands an
after-hours visitor an SMS/photo-triage path and says when a person is back.
Fixed a single-source violation while there: the booking engine carried its own
hardcoded hours table. Documented NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL as the Cal.com hook.

P1.8 Consented abandoned-quote recovery. QuoteRecovery model + migration, a
checkbox required by the schema (z.literal(true)), capture on pagehide, one
email after 2h via a CRON_SECRET-protected Vercel cron, sentAt stamped before
the send, and cancellation the moment the same address converts. No consent, no
send - CASL is not a style preference.

Also fixed: tsconfig.base.json was missing entirely (packages/shared extended a
file that did not exist; nothing read it until a test imported shared), and the
booking availability suite now passes with hours derived rather than typed.

ops/DOMINATION-RUNBOOK.md and ops/GA4-events.md added.

Verified: all 41 guards pass (39 existing + 2 new, both in the verify chain);
tsc error count identical to main (107, all sandbox-blocked Prisma engine, zero
in P1 files); 11/11 booking tests pass.

